TIP:  This song is all about the four-beat (D) (G) (A) (D) sequence.  It's not hard but notice that whenever the line ends in a (D), that (D) that just ended is the first (D) in the sequence.  For example "...the (D) mail (G) (A) (D)."

TIP:  In the chorus (if untransposed) you'll be playing a (G) and come across "(lift)".  This means to lift off the 1st string of the (G) as you need the (e).
 
 
